{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.4923082377196843, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The diff only changes the features (count fingerprints instead of bit fingerprints) and the KRR kernel. Nothing touches files, pastes answers or uses test labels.", "The MinMax kernel looks correct. For non-negative integer counts, sum over t=1..8 of [a>=t][b>=t] equals sum(min(a,b)) after capping at 8. The denominator sa+sb-smin equals sum(max). Both the train-train and test-train kernels apply the same cap. The kernel is positive semi-definite, so the solve is well-posed.", "Side effect: the features now cap counts at 255 and those counts also reach the RF and LGB models (assuming the same feature matrix feeds them). So the result is not a pure kernel ablation. The KRR kernel itself caps counts at 8. This does not invalidate the result. If Fa were scaled or standardized before minmax() the threshold trick would be wrong, but the diff gives no sign of that.", "Recomputed z = -(0.4923-0.4895)/(0.0042*sqrt(2)) \u2248 -0.47, which matches the harness value of -0.475. The candidate is 0.0028 worse than the incumbent, within noise with 1 run on each side. Reject is consistent with the numbers."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Switch the Morgan ECFP and FCFP features to clipped count fingerprints (max 255) and replace the Tanimoto kernel in the kernel-ridge member with a MinMax kernel computed from thresholded binary matmuls on counts capped at 8 (no chunking needed, since the matmul form never builds a 3D tensor).", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "cherry", "idea_id": "b024", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_lipo_HH_1_s1-candidate-11_1795051988980", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00306749, "cost_usd_plan": 0.003